From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zed-patches <zed-patches@localhost>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 19:00:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] agent_servers: zeo-lsp, the project's language servers for
 Claude Agent (Plus) over ACP
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Zeo proposal §6.13 (ask 5), the first cut of docs/SPIKE-6.13-LSP-OVER-MCP.md;
built with §6.69 as one story, on 0149's MCP-over-ACP plumbing. Claude Code
reads code through grep and file reads, while the language servers Zeo runs
for the project know where a symbol is defined, who uses it and what it is.
0002's IDE server was not the vehicle: the CLI keeps only getDiagnostics and
executeCode from it, and only for buffers already open.

zeo-lsp is one more acp declaration, after the proxied servers, answered by
Zeo itself (acp/zeo_lsp.rs, acp/zeo_lsp_tools.rs) instead of a context server:
server/discover, ping, tools/list and tools/call, five read-only tools --

  diagnostics { path? }        one file's entries (severity line:column:
                               message), or a count per file for the project
  definition  { path, line, symbol? | column? }   path:line: the defining line
  references  { path, line, symbol? | column? }   every use, path:line
  hover       { path, line, symbol? | column? }   the server's hover text
  document_symbols { path }    the outline, kind name Lstart-end, nested

Lines and columns are 1-based; without a column the symbol is found on its
line by name, the way the native agent's symbol_locator does. A file is
opened with its language servers for the call: open_buffer, then
register_buffer_with_language_servers -- Project::open_buffer_with_lsp is
test-support only, so a test build compiled it and a release build did not
(found by the z021 lane's first `cargo build -p zed`, 2026-11-22). A
failed lookup is the tool's own answer (isError, with the reason) so the
model reads why; an unknown tool is an MCP -32602 -- there is no rename,
edit or code action.

Declared only to an agent that advertised mcpCapabilities.acp, under the new
agent.zeo_lsp (default true: the operator's 2026-11-21 decision, on for Plus),
not for a remote project, not when a context server already has the name,
and only where the connection's McpProxyPolicy allows it -- so a jail
(0150) reaches it only through its opt-in list, like any proxied server.
agent.mcp_servers_over_acp no longer gates it: the two settings are separate.
0149's test harness turns it off, since those tests count the proxied servers.

What a cold file costs: a language server that has not indexed it can answer
empty, and many publish diagnostics only for open files; the instructions in
server/discover say so. Not in this cut: workspace symbols, call hierarchy,
type definition.

Tests zeo_lsp_tests (new; 0149's scripted agent, a fake language server with
the file already attached): discover and tools/list; not declared when off;
definition asks at the named symbol's position and answers path:line: line;
references, hover (by column) and document_symbols; diagnostics for a file
and for the project after a publishDiagnostics; a missing symbol is an
isError answer and an unknown tool -32602.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
